Rows as real apps hold them, through a rebuild: NULL and the empty string
apart, text in other scripts, emoji, a quote and a newline inside a value,
a long value, the largest integer, a real, and duplicates in a column that
allows them. Every value comes out as it went in.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, note TEXT, price INTEGER, weight REAL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'Smörgåsbord', NULL, 9223372036854775807, 0.1);
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (2, '', '', 0, -0.0);
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (3, '拉麵 🍜', 'it''s "hot"' || char(10) || 'mind the bowl', -1, 1e308);
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (4, 'soup', printf('%.1000c', 'x'), NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (5, 'soup', NULL, NULL, NULL);

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, note TEXT, price INTEGER, weight REAL, served TEXT) STRICT;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `dish`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "dish" RENAME TO "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, note TEXT, price INTEGER, weight REAL, served TEXT) STRICT
  table `dish`: its rows, by id, name, note, price, weight
    INSERT INTO "dish" ("id", "name", "note", "price", "weight") SELECT "id", "name", "note", "price", "weight" FROM "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_dish"

== query
SELECT id, quote(name), quote(substr(note, 1, 40)), length(note), price, weight FROM dish ORDER BY id

